# ---- RESEARCH CORPUS -- private in place (USER DECISION 2026-08-21, executed 2026-08-23) -----
# "research folder also get fully offline from public repo, what else?" -- recorded in
# research/findings/tooling/votv-ue4ss-f2-migration-DESIGN-2026-08-21.md:520-524 and NOT executed
# until 2026-08-23. 420 files / 24 MB of point-in-time RE, raw session logs, crash dumps and
# screenshots. It follows the site/ pattern: files STAY on disk with their own inner git repo, so
# every reading-order pointer still resolves locally and nothing is lost -- it is simply unpublished.
#
# WHAT THE DELAY COST (measured 2026-08-23, docs/DOCS_ARC.md §1d): the origin VPS IP was sitting in
# two tracked files -- research/crash_2026-07-03_rehost_wispkill/host_..._rehost_plain.log:11085-88
# (four lines, stun/turn/signaling) and votv-connection-selector-events-pinecone-2026-06-11.md:225.
# That is the SAME class as finding A11, which purged the IP from four docs on 2026-07-24 and whose
# sweep never crossed into research/. Plus three UE4Minidump.dmp process dumps of the user's own
# machine, contents unaudited. A leak sweep scoped to one directory is a leak sweep that has not run.
research/

# ---- SECURITY REGISTER -- a working exploit map for a SHIPPING mod ---------------------------
# docs/security/ is the finding register + fix plans: 18 OPEN rows of 33 carrying exact file:line and an
# explicit "attacker -> gain" column (wipe a stranger's persistent world; evict the real host and
# receive every joiner; drive another player's desk). On a PUBLIC repo that is a ready-made map
# against a mod real people are running right now. The files STAY on disk -- CLAUDE.md reading
# order 4f still resolves locally -- they are simply not published.
#
# THREE THINGS NOT TO RE-DERIVE (measured 2026-08-23, docs/DOCS_ARC.md §1):
#   - It WAS public for ~34 days (d95683cc, 2026-07-20 .. 2026-07-30, all on origin/main). The user
#     decided NOT to rewrite history, so this is casual-discoverability removal, not secrecy. Say
#     that plainly; never describe this ignore rule as having un-published anything.
#   - Removing the map does not shrink the attack surface by one byte. The cure is closing the
#     rows (docs/DOCS_ARC.md §5), and this rule must never be cited as "security handled".
#   - Source-file comments citing TRACKER rows over a SHIPPED fix are fine and deliberately kept:
#     attribution of a CLOSED finding reveals nothing. Only OPEN-count advertising is the problem.
# If a genuinely public security document is ever wanted, it goes to the root SECURITY.md instead.
docs/security/

# assets/paks -- TRACKED since 2026-09-01 (USER DIRECTIVE: "путь пак будет публичным и
# иконки и что требуется"). They were untracked as public-repo caution for game-derived
# meshes, and the caution bought less than it looked like: the ship decision
# (`docs/UE4SS_ARC.md` 7.6) already puts these exact bytes in every public release
# archive, so the ignore hid them from the repo and not from anyone. What it DID cost was
# the release lane -- `release-core.yml` publishes from a GitHub runner, where a fresh
# checkout has no paks, so an automated release would have shipped structurally correct
# and content-incomplete. `package.ps1 -Release` refuses that now, which made the
# automated lane unusable until these were tracked.
#
# One thing that IS newly true and was not before: git history is permanent. A release
# asset can be replaced; a committed blob stays reachable.
#
# The negation is per-extension rather than a bare `!assets/paks/**` so the global `*.pak`
# rule at the top of this file keeps covering every OTHER pak in the tree (the game's own,
# research/pak_re/, dev installs). Only this directory's contents are published.
!assets/paks/*.pak
!assets/paks/*.png
!assets/paks/README.md

# SUPPORT.md -- the Boosty working doc (2026-08-30, USER DIRECTIVE: gitignore it).
#
# It is the SOURCE the public donation copy is cut from: the page text in both languages, the
# tier ladder with its art direction, the placement plan, and the cost arithmetic behind the
# suggested prices. The arithmetic is the reason it stays local -- '26,000 roubles a month, so
# 29 backers at 900' is a useful number for the author and reads as a QUOTA on a public page,
# which turns a gift into a debt. What ships is a subset, pasted into Boosty, the README, the
# site and the Thunderstore README.
#
# NOTE the filename is not neutral: GitHub gives a TRACKED SUPPORT.md a native link from the
# repo's community profile and the new-issue page. Ignored, that link does not appear -- which
# is the intended trade here, not an oversight. If that link is wanted later, it should be a
# second SHORT tracked file, not this one.
#
# Same terms as its siblings above: the file stays ON DISK and every local pointer to it
# resolves; none resolves on GitHub.
SUPPORT.md



# Local-only: the CRUTCH REGISTER (USER 2026-09-04, "Crutches md пусть будет только локальным").
# Same reasoning as docs/security/ above, and the same terms: the file stays ON DISK, every local
# pointer to it resolves, none resolves on GitHub. It is a measured list of shipped weaknesses with
# the evidence for each -- C5 alone is an item-loss path a player can trigger -- so publishing it
# hands an attacker the map, which is the thing docs/security/ was untracked for on 2026-08-23.
# The three MARKDOWN LINKS to it (docs/README.md, docs/piles/README.md, docs/vehicles/ATV.md) were
# demoted to plain paths in the same commit: an unpublished target behind a live link is a 404 on
# GitHub, which is exactly the defect this session found on the website. Plain-text mentions in
# source comments and other docs are fine and were left -- they name a local doc, as CLAUDE.md does.
docs/CRUTCHES.md

# Local-only (USER 2026-09-04, in one instruction with CRUTCHES above). Same terms as every
# sibling in this block: each file stays ON DISK, every local pointer resolves, none resolves on
# GitHub.
